From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Freezer: support the cgroup v1 freezer

Freezer.isFreezerSupported() opens the file of the FreezerState
attribute and expects cgroup v2's cgroup.freeze, which reads "0" or
"1". On kernels without cgroup v2 the task profiles of this tree use the
v1 freezer instead (LOS-24.0 android_system_core patch 0002): frozen
processes are moved into /dev/freezer/frozen, a cgroup whose
freezer.state is set to FROZEN once by init, and FreezerState names
that file. It reads "FROZEN" (or "FREEZING" while tasks are on their way
into the refrigerator), so the check failed with "Unexpected value in
cgroup.freeze" and the app freezer stayed off.

When the attribute is a v1 freezer.state file, accept a state that
starts with 'F' and require a second thing: the framework kills frozen
processes without thawing them, and a stock v1 freezer keeps a killed
task frozen, memory and all, until its cgroup is thawed. Kernels that
let frozen tasks die say so in freezer.killable next to freezer.state
(kernel patch 0021 of this project; Android 11's kernels had the same
file). If the file is missing or does not read 1 the freezer stays off.

The remaining checks are unchanged: BINDER_GET_FROZEN_INFO has to work
and the Frozen and Unfrozen profiles have to be applicable, which for
the v1 profiles means that system_server can write to the cgroup.procs
files of /dev/freezer/frozen and /dev/freezer.

Nothing else in the framework needs the v2 file for freezing and
thawing: Process.setProcessFrozen() only applies the Frozen and
Unfrozen profiles. Two places still assume cgroup v2 and keep failing
the way they do without a v2 hierarchy: Process.freezeCgroupUid(), used
by ProcessList when it kills the processes of a package, now throws and
logs "Unable to freeze cgroup uid" where the empty profile used to
succeed without doing anything, and Process.isProcessFrozen() ("am
isfrozen") always answers false. Use "dumpsys activity" (section
"Apps frozen") or /dev/freezer/frozen/cgroup.procs to see what is
frozen.

Syntax-checked outside the build with stubbed headers; not built with
Soong, not run.

[combined set, 2026-11-06] Header only: the kernel patch number above is
that of the combined set (staging/backport-freezer: 0025). The diff is
unchanged.
---
 services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_Freezer.cpp | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_Freezer.cpp b/services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_Freezer.cpp
index e9a99f0..6322f4f 100644
--- a/services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_Freezer.cpp
+++ b/services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_Freezer.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <android-base/logging.h>
+#include <android-base/strings.h>
 #include <android-base/unique_fd.h>
 #include <binder/IPCThreadState.h>
 #include <nativehelper/JNIHelp.h>
@@ -45,6 +46,37 @@ jint freezeBinder(JNIEnv* env, jobject, jint pid, jboolean freeze, jint timeout_
     return retVal;
 }
 
+// Cgroup v1 freezer (kernels without cgroup v2). The FreezerState attribute is then the
+// freezer.state file of the cgroup that frozen processes are moved into, and reads "FROZEN"
+// (or "FREEZING" while tasks are on their way into the refrigerator) once init has set the
+// cgroup up. The framework kills frozen processes without thawing them first, which the v1
+// freezer only supports when the kernel says so in the cgroup's freezer.killable file.
+bool isLegacyFreezerUsable(const std::string& statePath, char state) {
+    if (state != 'F') {
+        ALOGE("Unexpected value in %s: %d", statePath.c_str(), state);
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    const size_t slash = statePath.rfind('/');
+    if (slash == std::string::npos) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    const std::string killablePath = statePath.substr(0, slash) + "/freezer.killable";
+    base::unique_fd fd(open(killablePath.c_str(), O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC));
+    if (fd < 0) {
+        ALOGE("Cannot open \"%s\": %s; frozen processes could not be killed, not using the "
+              "freezer", killablePath.c_str(), strerror(errno));
+        return false;
+    }
+    char killable;
+    if (::read(fd, &killable, 1) != 1 || killable != '1') {
+        ALOGE("Frozen processes are not killable according to %s, not using the freezer",
+              killablePath.c_str());
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
 jint getBinderFreezeInfo(JNIEnv *env, jobject, jint pid) {
     uint32_t syncReceived = 0, asyncReceived = 0;
 
@@ -83,7 +115,11 @@ bool isFreezerSupported(JNIEnv *env, jclass) {
         ALOGI("Failed to read freezer state: %s", strerror(errno));
         return false;
     }
-    if (state != '1' && state != '0') {
+    if (base::EndsWith(path, "/freezer.state")) {
+        if (!isLegacyFreezerUsable(path, state)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    } else if (state != '1' && state != '0') {
         ALOGE("Unexpected value in cgroup.freeze: %d", state);
         return false;
     }
